---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"

const repo = "https://github.com/kylemclaren/jevql"
const install = "brew install kylemclaren/tap/jevql"
---

<Layout>
  <main class="page">
    <header class="mast">
      <a class="brand" href="./">jevql</a>
      <div class="mast-right">
        <span class="tagline">Semantic SQL for vanilla Postgres</span>
        <a class="repo-link" href={repo} aria-label="GitHub repository">
          <svg class="gh" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z"/></svg>
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">A psql-shaped CLI · no Postgres extension required</p>
      <h1>Ask your database <mark>a real question.</mark></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Put <code>jev(people, 'could work from home')</code> in a WHERE clause. Postgres runs the SQL,
        Jev judges the rows, you get a psql table. No extension to install: the server only sees plain SQL.
      </p>
      <div class="install-cta">
        <button id="download" type="button">
          <span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">download</span> download jevql
        </button>
        <button class="secondary copy" type="button" data-copy={install}>
          <span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span> {install}
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="truth-strip">
        <span>works on any postgres</span><span>no extension</span><span>no proxy</span><span>answers cached</span><span>$0.042 / M tokens</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <dialog id="dl" aria-labelledby="dl-title">
      <div class="dl-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">download</p><h2 id="dl-title">Get jevql</h2></div>
        <button id="dl-close" class="secondary" type="button" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
      </div>
      <p class="dl-version">latest release: <strong id="dl-tag">…</strong></p>
      <div class="dl-curl">
        <small>one line, detects your platform</small>
        <div class="dl-curl-row">
          <code id="curl-line">curl -fsSL …/install.sh | sh</code>
          <button class="secondary copy small" type="button" data-copy-from="curl-line" aria-label="Copy install command"><span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span></button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="dl-or">or pick a tarball</p>
      <div class="dl-grid" id="dl-grid">
        {[
          ["darwin", "arm64", "macOS", "Apple Silicon"],
          ["darwin", "amd64", "macOS", "Intel"],
          ["linux", "amd64", "Linux", "x86_64"],
          ["linux", "arm64", "Linux", "arm64"],
        ].map(([os, arch, label, name]) => (
          <div class="dl-tile" data-os={os} data-arch={arch}>
            <small>{label}</small>
            <strong>{name}</strong>
            <div class="dl-actions">
              <a class="dl-get" href={`${repo}/releases/latest`} download><span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">download</span> download</a>
              <button class="dl-copy copy small" type="button" data-copy="" aria-label={`Copy ${label} ${name} link`}><span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">link</span></button>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Tarballs contain the <code>jevql</code> binary; unpack it onto your PATH. Checksums are on the <a href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}>release page</a>.</p>
    </dialog>

    <section class="examples" aria-label="Examples">
      <div class="examples-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">examples · <span id="ex-name">people</span></p>
        <div class="dots" id="ex-dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Pick an example"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="race">
        <article class="lane direct">
          <div class="lane-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">you type</p><h2>SQL, with one new function</h2></div><span class="badge">query</span></div>
          <pre class="output" id="ex-query"></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="lane generated">
          <div class="lane-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">you get</p><h2>A table, and the bill</h2></div><span class="badge pink">result</span></div>
          <pre class="output" id="ex-result"></pre>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="meter ex-meter" aria-hidden="true"><i id="ex-progress"></i></div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-map" aria-label="How a query runs">
      <div><small>1 / collect</small><strong>Postgres runs your SQL with the jev terms stripped. Indexed filters stay on the server.</strong></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div class="method-model"><small>2 / judge</small><strong>Surviving rows go to TypeSafe in batches. Identical rows are judged once and cached.</strong></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div><small>3 / project</small><strong>Filter, sort, group and limit happen in the CLI. You get a psql table.</strong></div>
    </section>

    <section class="machine" aria-labelledby="functions-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">functions</p><h2 id="functions-title">Same names as pg-jev</h2></div>
        <a class="repo-link" href={`${repo}#sql-surface`}>full surface ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="phases" aria-label="Functions">
        <div class="phase"><small>boolean</small><strong>jev()</strong><span><code>jev(p, 'condition' [, 0.7])</code><br />A calibrated probability against a threshold. Works in WHERE, also as <code>NOT jev()</code>.</span></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>numbers</small><strong>jev_prob() · jev_score()</strong><span><code>jev_prob(p, 'condition')</code> → 0..1<br /><code>jev_score(p, 'q', ARRAY['lo','mid','hi'])</code> → weighted level</span></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>labels</small><strong>jev_choice()</strong><span><code>jev_choice(t, 'which team?', ARRAY['billing','technical'])</code><br />Works with GROUP BY and count(*).</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Send fewer columns with <code>jev((name, bio), '…')</code>. Anything without <code>jev_*</code> passes straight through, so it doubles as a plain psql.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="machine" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">install</p><h2 id="install-title">One binary, then just type <code>jevql</code></h2></div>
        <a class="repo-link" href={`${repo}/releases`}>releases ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="phases" aria-label="Install options">
        <div class="phase"><small>shell</small><pre class="output" id="curl-line-2">curl -fsSL …/install.sh | sh</pre></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>homebrew</small><pre class="output">brew install kylemclaren/tap/jevql</pre></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>go</small><pre class="output">go install github.com/kylemclaren/jevql/cmd/jevql@latest</pre><span>needs CGO for the Postgres parser</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">First launch asks for a database URL and a TypeSafe key and saves them to <code>~/.config/jevql/env</code>. Or use <code>DATABASE_URL</code>, <code>PG*</code> and <code>TYPESAFE_API_KEY</code> like any psql user.</p>
    </section>

    <details>
      <summary>Read before pointing it at real data</summary>
      <div class="details-grid">
        <p><b>Row contents go to TypeSafe.</b> Every column of the judged alias is sent over HTTPS. Narrow it with <code>jev((name, bio), …)</code> or <code>--columns</code>.</p>
        <p><b>It scans everything your SQL filters let through.</b> Put cheap predicates first. <code>--explain</code> shows the collect SQL, row count and cost with no API call; <code>--max-rows</code> aborts before HTTP.</p>
        <p><b>Not an extension.</b> <code>jev()</code> exists only inside this CLI. Apps sending it through JDBC will fail. The names mirror pg-jev, so moving later is a rename.</p>
        <p><b>The cache is a local sqlite file.</b> Keyed by model, question and canonical row JSON. Mode 0600, no expiry. <code>\cache clear</code> or <code>--no-cache</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <footer>
      <span>jevQL · MIT</span>
      <span><a href={repo}>GitHub</a> · <a href="https://typesafe.ai">TypeSafe</a> · <a href="https://github.com/realZachi/pg-jev">pg-jev</a> · styled after <a href="https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev">openjev</a></span>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <script>
    const repo = "https://github.com/kylemclaren/jevql"
    const reduced = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches

    // ---- copy buttons -------------------------------------------------
    function flash(btn: HTMLElement, ok = true) {
      const original = btn.innerHTML
      btn.innerHTML = `<span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">${ok ? "check" : "close"}</span>${btn.classList.contains("small") ? "" : " copied"}`
      setTimeout(() => (btn.innerHTML = original), 1200)
    }
    document.addEventListener("click", async (e) => {
      const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>(".copy")
      if (!btn) return
      const from = btn.dataset.copyFrom
      const text = from ? document.getElementById(from)?.textContent || "" : btn.dataset.copy || ""
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text)
        flash(btn)
      } catch {
        flash(btn, false)
      }
    })

    // ---- install command reflects where the site is hosted -------------
    const curl = `curl -fsSL ${location.origin}/install.sh | sh`
    for (const id of ["curl-line", "curl-line-2"]) {
      const el = document.getElementById(id)
      if (el) el.textContent = curl
    }

    // ---- download dialog -----------------------------------------------
    const dl = document.getElementById("dl") as HTMLDialogElement | null
    const tagEl = document.getElementById("dl-tag")
    let loaded = false
    async function loadRelease() {
      if (loaded) return
      loaded = true
      try {
        const r = await fetch("https://api.github.com/repos/kylemclaren/jevql/releases/latest", { headers: { Accept: "application/vnd.github+json" } })
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error(String(r.status))
        const rel = await r.json()
        const tag: string = rel.tag_name
        const ver = tag.replace(/^v/, "")
        if (tagEl) tagEl.textContent = tag
        for (const tile of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".dl-tile")) {
          const name = `jevql_${ver}_${tile.dataset.os}_${tile.dataset.arch}.tar.gz`
          const asset = (rel.assets || []).find((x: { name: string }) => x.name === name)
          const url = asset ? asset.browser_download_url : `${repo}/releases/download/${tag}/${name}`
          const a = tile.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>(".dl-get")
          if (a) { a.href = url; a.setAttribute("download", name) }
          const c = tile.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".dl-copy")
          if (c) c.dataset.copy = url
        }
      } catch {
        if (tagEl) tagEl.textContent = "see releases page"
      }
    }
    const ua = navigator.userAgent
    const guessOS = /Mac/i.test(ua) ? "darwin" : /Linux|Android/i.test(ua) ? "linux" : ""
    const guessArch = /arm64|aarch64/i.test(ua) ? "arm64" : "amd64"
    document.querySelector(`.dl-tile[data-os="${guessOS}"][data-arch="${guessArch}"]`)?.classList.add("likely")
    document.getElementById("download")?.addEventListener("click", () => { loadRelease(); dl?.showModal() })
    document.getElementById("dl-close")?.addEventListener("click", () => dl?.close())
    dl?.addEventListener("click", (e) => { if (e.target === dl) dl.close() })

    // ---- rotating examples ---------------------------------------------
    type Example = { name: string; query: string; result: string }
    const examples: Example[] = [
      {
        name: "people",
        query: `SELECT name, city,
       jev_prob(people, 'could work from home') AS p
FROM people
WHERE jev(people, 'could work from home')
  AND country = 'PT'
ORDER BY p DESC
LIMIT 20;`,
        result: `     name      |  city  |  p
---------------+--------+------
 Miguel Costa  | Lisbon | 0.94
 Ada Fernandes | Lisbon | 0.93
 Pedro Martins | Lisbon | 0.91
(3 rows)

jev: 6 judged, 1 req, 0 cache hits, 1.2k tokens, $0.0001, 1.35s`,
      },
      {
        name: "support tickets",
        query: `SELECT jev_choice(tickets, 'which team should handle this?',
                  ARRAY['billing','technical','sales']) AS team,
       count(*)
FROM tickets
WHERE status = 'open'
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC;`,
        result: `   team    | count
-----------+-------
 technical |     3
 sales     |     3
 billing   |     1
(3 rows)

jev: 7 judged, 1 req, 0 cache hits, 1.2k tokens, $0.0001, 0.75s`,
      },
      {
        name: "movies",
        query: `SELECT title, year
FROM movies
WHERE jev(movies, 'a safe pick for a first date')
  AND year >= 2010
ORDER BY year DESC
LIMIT 4;`,
        result: `          title          | year
-------------------------+------
 Past Lives              | 2023
 The Big Sick            | 2017
 About Time              | 2013
 Silver Linings Playbook | 2012
(4 rows)

jev: 412 judged, 11 req, 0 cache hits, 61.3k tokens, $0.0026, 4.1s`,
      },
      {
        name: "inbox",
        query: `SELECT sender, subject
FROM emails
WHERE NOT jev(emails, 'a newsletter or promotion')
  AND received > now() - interval '1 day'
ORDER BY received DESC;`,
        result: `     sender      |            subject
-----------------+--------------------------------
 Joana Silva     | Re: Q4 hiring plan
 Ravi Patel      | Invoice #4821 corrected
 Ada Fernandes   | Can we ship Friday?
(3 rows)

jev: 58 judged, 2 req, 21 cache hits, 5.9k tokens, $0.0002, 1.9s`,
      },
      {
        name: "reviews",
        query: `SELECT product,
       jev_score(reviews, 'how angry is the customer?',
                 ARRAY['calm','annoyed','furious']) AS anger
FROM reviews
WHERE stars <= 2
ORDER BY anger DESC
LIMIT 3;`,
        result: `    product     | anger
----------------+-------
 Cold brew kit  |  1.96
 Desk lamp v2   |  1.41
 Wool socks     |  0.87
(3 rows)

jev: 133 judged, 4 req, 0 cache hits, 21.0k tokens, $0.0009, 2.6s`,
      },
      {
        name: "recipes",
        query: `SELECT name, jev_prob(recipes, 'kid friendly') AS p
FROM recipes
WHERE jev((name, ingredients), 'vegetarian')
ORDER BY p DESC
LIMIT 3;`,
        result: `        name         |  p
---------------------+------
 Mac and cheese      | 0.97
 Margherita pizza    | 0.95
 Lentil shepherd pie | 0.62
(3 rows)

jev: 240 judged, 6 req, 120 cache hits, 17.8k tokens, $0.0007, 2.2s`,
      },
    ]

    const q = document.getElementById("ex-query")!
    const res = document.getElementById("ex-result")!
    const nameEl = document.getElementById("ex-name")!
    const dots = document.getElementById("ex-dots")!
    const bar = document.getElementById("ex-progress") as HTMLElement
    const HOLD = 7000
    let idx = 0, run = 0, paused = false, timer: number | undefined

    examples.forEach((ex, i) => {
      const b = document.createElement("button")
      b.type = "button"
      b.role = "tab"
      b.setAttribute("aria-label", ex.name)
      b.addEventListener("click", () => show(i, true))
      dots.appendChild(b)
    })

    function setBar(active: boolean) {
      bar.style.transition = "none"
      bar.style.width = "0%"
      if (!active) return
      requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        bar.style.transition = `width ${HOLD}ms linear`
        bar.style.width = "100%"
      }))
    }

    async function show(i: number, manual = false) {
      const my = ++run
      if (timer) clearTimeout(timer)
      idx = i
      const ex = examples[i]
      nameEl.textContent = ex.name
      dots.querySelectorAll("button").forEach((b, j) => b.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(j === i)))
      res.classList.remove("show")
      res.textContent = ex.result
      setBar(false)
      if (reduced || manual) {
        q.textContent = ex.query
      } else {
        q.textContent = ""
        q.classList.add("typing")
        for (let n = 1; n <= ex.query.length; n++) {
          if (my !== run) return
          q.textContent = ex.query.slice(0, n)
          const ch = ex.query[n - 1]
          await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ch === "\n" ? 90 : 12))
        }
        q.classList.remove("typing")
        await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 250))
        if (my !== run) return
      }
      res.classList.add("show")
      setBar(true)
      timer = window.setTimeout(() => { if (!paused) show((idx + 1) % examples.length) }, HOLD)
    }
    const wrap = document.querySelector(".examples")!
    wrap.addEventListener("mouseenter", () => { paused = true })
    wrap.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { paused = false; if (!timer) show((idx + 1) % examples.length) })
    show(0, true)
  </script>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  code { font: inherit; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-weight: 800; }
  .lede code { font-size: .9em; }
  .install-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; margin: 6px 0 26px; }
  .install-cta button { text-transform: none; padding: 18px 24px; font-size: .92rem; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink); }
  .install-cta button .material-symbols-rounded { font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .install-cta button:active:not(:disabled) { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 750px) { .install-cta { flex-direction: column; } .install-cta button { width: 100%; } }
  button.secondary { background: #fff; }
  button.secondary:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--lime); }
  button.small { padding: 8px 9px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  .mast .repo-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .section-head { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .section-head h2 code { font: inherit; }

  /* examples */
  .examples { margin-top: 24px; }
  .examples-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .examples-head .eyebrow { margin: 0; }
  .examples-head #ex-name { color: var(--pink); }
  .dots { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
  .dots button, .dots button:where(button) { width: 12px; height: 12px; min-height: 0; padding: 0; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: #fff; box-shadow: none; }
  @media (max-width: 750px) { .dots button { min-height: 0; height: 12px; width: 12px; } }
  .dots button[aria-selected="true"] { background: var(--lime); }
  .race { margin-top: 0; }
  .lane { min-height: 0; }
  .lane .output { margin: 14px 0 0; border: 0; padding: 0; min-height: 11.5em; }
  #ex-query.typing::after { content: "▍"; color: var(--pink); animation: blink 1s steps(2) infinite; }
  #ex-result { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); transition: opacity .35s ease, transform .35s ease; }
  #ex-result.show { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .ex-meter { margin: 10px 0 0; }
  @keyframes blink { 50% { opacity: 0; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { #ex-result { transition: none; } #ex-query.typing::after { animation: none; } }

  /* method map */
  .method-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; }
  .method-map strong { font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.45; }
  @media (max-width: 750px) { .method-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* panels */
  .phase .output { margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: .66rem; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .phase strong { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .phase span { margin-top: 8px; }
  .phase span code { font-weight: 800; }

  /* dialog */
  dialog { position: fixed; inset: 0; margin: auto; max-height: calc(100vh - 40px); overflow: auto; width: min(600px, calc(100% - 28px)); border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 0; background: var(--panel); color: var(--ink); padding: 22px; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--ink); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
  dialog::backdrop { background: rgba(23, 23, 21, .55); }
  .dl-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; }
  .dl-head h2 { margin: 0; font: 900 1.6rem/1 Arial, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .dl-version { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-curl { margin-top: 14px; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: var(--lime); padding: 12px; }
  .dl-curl small { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: .58rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-curl-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .dl-curl-row code { flex: 1; font-size: .72rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .dl-or { margin: 14px 0 8px; font-size: .62rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .dl-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  .dl-tile { border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: #fff; padding: 12px; }
  .dl-tile.likely { box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink); }
  .dl-tile small { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; font-size: .58rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-tile strong { display: block; font-size: .95rem; }
  .dl-actions { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin-top: 10px; }
  .dl-get { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; flex: 1; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: var(--lime); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); padding: 8px 10px; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-get:active { transform: translate(1px, 1px); box-shadow: 1px 1px 0 var(--ink); }
  .dl-copy { background: #fff; }
  dialog .fine { margin-top: 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .dl-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
